  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For collaborative workspaces in such as painting rooms or worlds with resource intensive interactables, sometimes blocking a problematic user is not enough and also sometimes it may be too much of an escalation to kick someone from an instance. \n\nPlease implement a feature that allows users to remove the ability for interaction from a user. \n\nI think the threshold for this should be lower than a kick, whatever the rules for kicks are at the moment. I am also suggesting a system that takes cumulative time spent in the world into account, giving the natives, so to speak, a bit more control over the space.\n\nConsider allowing the instance host the ability to reinstate interaction privileges for moderated persons.",
